speechtext:
That the House concur in Interim Supply as follows:
That a sum not exceeding $13,144,733,701.68 being composed of:
(1)	three-twelfths ($9,810,806,535.00) of the total of the amounts of the items set forth in the Main Estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1992, which were laid upon the Table Thursday, February 28,1991, except for Parliament Vote 5 which was ordered deleted from the Estimates by the Speaker on Wednesday, March 20, 1991 and except those items below;
(2)	eleven-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Transport Vote 15, and Treasury Board Vote 10 (Schedule A) of the said Estimates, $171,116,000.00;
(3)	nine-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Employment and Immigration Vote 20, and Treasury Board Vote 5 (Schedule B) of the said Estimates, $305,918,250.00;
(4)	eight-twelfths of the total of the amount of Agriculture Vote 30 (Schedule C) of the said Estimates, $29,896,000.00;
(5)	six-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Indian Affairs and Northern Development Vote 40, and Labour Vote 15, and Secretary of State Vote 20 (Schedule D) of the said Estimates, $156,326,500.00;
(6)	five-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Communications Vote 45, and Indian Affairs and Northern Development Votes 15 and 45, and Industry, Science and Technology Vote 45, and Transport Vote 1 (Schedule E) of the said Estimates, $1,568,493,750.00; and
(7)	four-twelfths of the total of the amounts of Communications Votes 25, 30, 55 and 70, and Consumer and Corporate Affairs Votes 1 and 20, and Energy, Mines and Resources Vote 35, and Environment Vote 1, and Finance Vote 25, and Indian Affairs and Northern Development Vote 30, and Industry, Science and Technology Votes 40 and 100, and Justice Vote 1, and Labour Vote
Supply
5, and National Health and Welfare Vote 15, and National Revenue Vote 5, and Privy Council Vote 1, and Secretary of State Vote 15, and Solicitor General Vote 1, and Supply and Services Vote 1, and Transport Vote 35 (Schedule F) of the said Estimates, $1,102,176,666.68;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending March 31, 1992.
